; coop_phantom.ltx
; Visual stand-in for a remote player, puppeted every frame by coop_phantom.script
; from network position/rotation samples (see coop_actor_sync.script).
;
; Inherits the stock [stalker] class wholesale (gamedata/configs/creatures/m_stalker.ltx
; in the base Anomaly install) rather than a custom native class, so spawning only
; needs the well-established alife_create() path. Known limitations, acceptable for
; this phase and worth revisiting later:
;   - this is an ordinary ALife object and currently WILL be written into the host's
;     savegame (no can_save()-style override yet, see se_projector.script for the
;     pattern to add one later).
;   - its own AI/behavior tree keeps running underneath; nothing suppresses it, so it
;     can still look around / react to nearby danger between position corrections.
;     coop_phantom.script overrides position/rotation/animation every frame from its
;     own actor_on_update tick (see update_phantoms() there) -- not a per-NPC hook,
;     since RegisterScriptCallback("npc_on_update", ...) turned out to never fire.
[coop_phantom]:stalker
$spawn = "stalkers\coop_phantom"
